{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Who built, </b>who planted, who betrothed — the Rabbis taught: the Torah taught derekh eretz, that a person should build a house and plant a vineyard and afterward betroth a woman. And so our Rabbis said elsewhere: 'Prepare your work outside' — this is a house; 'and ready it for yourself in the field' — this is a vineyard; 'afterward you shall build your house' — this is a wife. And in order to frighten them in war, Moses mentioned these three. And since from these three he had admonished them in parashat Ki Tavo — 'a wife he shall betroth, a house he shall build, a vineyard he shall plant' — they would ponder in their hearts: if a mishap occurs to them in war because of the curse of Moses, it is to instill in the sinners [the desire] to return." "<b>Let him go and return to his house, lest he die.</b> For all his heart and desire is to complete what he began, and his heart is not on the war; therefore he will flee and cause others to flee." "<b>Yachanchenu (dedicate it).</b> The ḥet with a shva."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:30.354446068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}